 ## Subtopics
 
 ### DWTGS
-DWTGS is a variant that rethinks frequency regularization specifically for sparse-view 3D Gaussian Splatting [S2, unofficial]. It applies a Discrete Wavelet Transform (DWT) to the rendered image and penalizes the loss in the wavelet domain [S2, unofficial]. This approach encourages sharper edges compared to standard frequency regularization methods [S2, unofficial]. It is chosen when working with sparse input views where edge definition is critical [S2, unofficial].
+DWTGS is a variant designed for sparse-view 3D Gaussian Splatting [S2, unofficial]. It rethinks frequency regularization by applying a Discrete Wavelet Transform (DWT) on the rendered image and penalizing the loss in the wavelet domain [S2, unofficial]. This approach encourages sharper edges compared to standard Fourier-based methods, which is particularly beneficial when training data is limited [S2, unofficial].
 
 ## Operating characteristics
-**Time and Memory Complexity:**
-*   **Time:** Adds the computational cost of the frequency transform (e.g., FFT or DWT) and loss calculation per training step. Not given in the sources.
